ations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrabino1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrabino1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrabino1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrabino1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"unsubscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2026-06-29T13:46:58Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4846414661","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/3355#issuecomment-4846414661","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3355","id":4846414661,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz888AAAABIN5rRQ","user":{"login":"maximilize","id":3752128,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTIxMjg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3752128?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximilize","html_url":"https://github.com/maximilize","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximilize/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximilize/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximilize/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximilize/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximilize/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximilize/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximilize/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximilize/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximilize/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-30T17:53:14Z","updated_at":"2026-06-30T17:53:14Z","body":"This is a regression in what `policy check` does, not a connectivity issue. In 0.28.0 the command validated the file **offline**, with no server and no database:\n\n```go\n// v0.28.0 cmd/headscale/cli/policy.go\n_, err = policy.NewPolicyManager(policyBytes, nil, views.Slice[types.NodeView]{})\n```\n\nSince 0.29 it instead calls a running headscale over the API (`cmd/headscale/cli/policy.go`, `checkPolicy.RunE` → `withClient(... CheckPolicyWithResponse ...)`), which is the socket/`context deadline exceeded` you hit without a server.\n\nThe `--bypass-server-and-access-database-directly` flag added after 0.29.1 doesn't cover this case either: `openBypassDB` (`policy.go:42`) prompts interactively (`[y/n]`, so it aborts under CI/closed stdin) and then needs a full config + an existing database — not an offline file check.\n\nReproduced with the official images, no server and no DB:\n\n```\n$ headscale:0.28.0 policy check --file policy.hujson   → Policy is valid        (exit 0)\n$ headscale:0.29.1 policy check --file policy.hujson   → context deadline exceeded (exit 1)\n```\n\nA `main` build behaves the same: default → API timeout; `--bypass…` → interactive prompt, then `Fatal config error` without a config/DB.\n\nThe 0.28 path — a structural parse via `NewPolicyManager(bytes, nil, <empty nodes>)`, needing neither server nor DB — is what CI use needs. Restoring it as a parse-only path is a small change; I can open a PR for it.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4846414661/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"maximilize","id":3752128,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTIxMjg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3752128?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximilize","html_url":"https://github.com/maximilize","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximilize/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximilize/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maximiliz